 of the questions are {s1}, and the rest are equally divided as {s2} and {s3} questions. If {name} is sure to get {r1}% of the {s1} questions, and {frac} of the {s2} and {s3} questions correctly, the total points she is sure to get is <<(r1 / 100) * n * 1 + (frac / 100) * n * (2 * 1)>>. The final answer is <<(r1 / 100) * n * 1 + (frac / 100) * n * (2 * 1)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 20, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['mult', 'n1', 'n2'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 21, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. Initially, {name} picked {n1} {fruit} on {d1}. Then he picked {n2} {fruit} on {d2}. On {d3}, he picked {mult} times the number of {fruit} he did on {d1}, which is <<mult * n1>>. The total is <<n1 + n2 + mult * n1>>. The final answer is <<n1 + n2 + mult * n1>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 22, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['ans', 'h1', 'h2', 'h3', 'm1', 'm2', 'n2', 'total'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 23, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. On {d1} and {d2}, he watched a {h1}-hour episode each night, so he watched <<2 * h1>> hours in total. On {d3}, he watched a few episodes of a {m1}-minute show, so he watched <<m1 / 60>> episodes. On {d4}, he watched a {h2}-hour episode and a {m2}-minute show, so he watched <<h2 + m2 / 60>> hours in total. On {d5}, he got to stay up late, so he watched {n2} {h3}-hour episodes, so he watched <<n2 * h3>> hours in total. The total hours of TV he watched is <<2 * h1 + m1 / 60 + h2 + m2 / 60 + n2 * h3>>. The number of {m1}-minute episodes he watched on {d3} is <<(total - 2 * h1 - m1 / 60 - h2 - m2 / 60 - n2 * h3) * 60 / m1>>. The final answer is <<(total - 2 * h1 - m1 / 60 - h2 - m2 / 60 - n2 * h3) * 60 / m1>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 24, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['p1', 'p2', 'total'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 25, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. First, we need to find out how many students are in the first group. {p1}% of the class are in the first group, so the number of students in the first group is <<total * p1 / 100>>. The remaining students are <<total - total * p1 / 100>>. Out of these remaining students, {p2}% are in the second group or part of the third group, so the number of students in the second group or part of the third group is <<(total - total * p1 / 100) * p2 / 100>>. The total number of students leaving early is <<(total - total * p1 / 100) * (1 - p2 / 100)>>. The final answer is <<(total - total * p1 / 100) * (1 - p2 / 100)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 26, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['n1', 'n2', 'n3'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 27, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name1} eats {n1} {food} per {time_unit}, so in one week, he eats <<n1 * 7>> {food}. {name2} eats {n2} {food} per {time_unit}, so in one week, he eats <<n2 * 7>> {food}. {name3} eats {n3} {food} per {time_unit}, so in one week, he eats <<n3 * 7>> {food}. The total amount of {food} eaten by the family in one week is <<n1 * 7 + n2 * 7 + n3 * 7>>. The final answer is <<n1 * 7 + n2 * 7 + n3 * 7>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 28, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['d', 'n', 'p'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 29, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name} gets {n} emails a day. {p}% of those emails don't require any response, so {p/100} of them do. The number of emails he responds to is <<n * (1 - p/100)>>. The final answer is <<n * (1 - p/100)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 30, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['age1', 'mult', 'years'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 31, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name1} is {age1} years old. In {years} years, {name1} will be <<age1 + years>> years old. {name2} will be {mult} times as old as {name1} is now, so {name2} will be <<mult * age1>> years old in {years} years. The current age of {name2} is <<mult * age1 - years>>. The final answer is <<mult * age1 - years>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 32, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['age1', 'age_diff'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 33, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The difference in age between {name1} and {name2} is {age_diff} years. Since {name1} is younger than {name2}, we can write the equation <<age1 + age_diff/2>>. The final answer is <<age1 + age_diff/2>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 34, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['goal', 'n1', 'n2', 's1', 's2'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 35, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. Initially, {name1} has {s1} signatures and {name2} has {s2} signatures. After {n1} weeks, they have a total of <<s1 + s2>> signatures. They have {n2} more weeks of {vacation_type}, and they want to reach {goal} signatures between them. The total number of signatures they need to collect is <<goal - (s1 + s2)>>. The final answer is <<goal - (s1 + s2)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 36, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['fee1_percent', 'fee2_percent', 'loan', 'price'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 37, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The selling price of the property is ${price}. The fees are {fee1_percent}% of the selling price, which is <<price * fee1_percent / 100>>. The fees are also {fee2_percent}% of the selling price, which is <<price * fee2_percent / 100>>. The total fees are <<price * (fee1_percent + fee2_percent) / 100>>. The remaining amount after paying the fees is <<price - (price * (fee1_percent + fee2_percent) / 100)>>. The loan amount is ${loan}. The net proceeds are <<price - (price * (fee1_percent + fee2_percent) / 100) - loan>>. The final answer is <<price - (price * (fee1_percent + fee2_percent) / 100) - loan>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 38, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['n1', 'n2', 'price1', 'price2'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 39, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The cost of {n1} loaves of {item1} is <<n1 * price1>>. The cost of {n2} {item2} is <<n2 * price2>>. The difference in cost is <<n1 * price1 - n2 * price2>>. The final answer is <<n1 * price1 - n2 * price2>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 40, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['discount', 'k', 'n1', 'n12', 'n2', 'n3', 'p1', 'p2', 'p3', 'total'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 41, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. Initially, {name} had {cur}{total} to buy whatever she wanted. At the {shop}, she bought {n12} {unit}s of {item1} at {cur}{p1} per {unit}, with a discount of {n2} {unit}s {discount}. The total cost of the {item1} is <<n12 * (p1 - (n2 * p1 / 100))>>. The mixed bag of {item2} and {item3} costs <<n3 * (p2 + p3)>>. The total cost is <<n12 * (p1 - (n2 * p1 / 100)) + n3 * (p2 + p3)>>. The remaining money is <<total - (n12 * (p1 - (n2 * p1 / 100)) + n3 * (p2 + p3))>>. The final answer is <<total - (n12 * (p1 - (n2 * p1 / 100)) + n3 * (p2 + p3))>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 42, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['frac', 'n'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 43, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name} found {frac} as many {insect1} as {insect2} in the {location}. If there were {n} {insect2}, the number of {insect1} is <<frac * n>>. The total number of insects is <<n + frac * n>>. The final answer is <<n + frac * n>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 44, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['faculty', 'graduates', 'total'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 45, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The total number of seats available is <<total - graduates - faculty>>. Each graduate would receive <<(total - graduates - faculty) / graduates>> tickets. The final answer is <<(total - graduates - faculty) / graduates>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 46, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['frac', 'mult1', 'n', 'x', 'y'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 47, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. Initially, {name1} hid {n} dozen eggs, which is <<12 * n>>. {name2} finds {x} eggs. {name3} finds {mult1} as many as {name2}, which is <<x * mult1>>. {name4} finds {y} less than {name3}, which is <<x * mult1 - y>>. {name5} finds {frac} as many as {name4}, which is <<(x * mult1 - y) * frac>>. The total number of eggs found is <<x * mult1 + (x * mult1 - y) + ((x * mult1 - y) * frac)>>. The remaining eggs are <<12 * n - (x * mult1 + (x * mult1 - y) + ((x * mult1 - y) * frac))>>. The final answer is <<12 * n - (x * mult1 + (x * mult1 - y) + ((x * mult1 - y) * frac))>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 48, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['area', 'length'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 49, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The area of a rectangle is given by <<length * 3.28125 * 3.28125>> square feet. The perimeter of a rectangle is given by <<2 * (length + 3.28125 * 3.28125)>> feet. The final answer is <<2 * (length + 3.28125 * 3.28125)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 50, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['n1', 'n2', 'n3', 'p1', 'p2', 'p3'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 51, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The price of {item1} is {cur}{p1} per {unit}, so the total revenue from {item1} is <<n1 * p1>>. The price of {item2} is {cur}{p2} per {unit}, so the total revenue from {item2} is <<n2 * p2>>. The price of {item3} is {cur}{p3} per {unit}, so the total revenue from {item3} is <<n3 * p3>>. The total revenue is <<n1 * p1 + n2 * p2 + n3 * p3>>. The final answer is <<n1 * p1 + n2 * p2 + n3 * p3>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 52, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['frac', 'n1', 'n2'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 53, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name2} scored {n2} points more than {frac} as many as {name1}, which means {name2} scored <<n2 + (n1 / frac)>> points. The total points scored by both is <<n1 + n2 + (n1 / frac)>>. The final answer is <<n1 + n2 + (n1 / frac)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 54, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['n1', 'n2', 'n3', 'total'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 55, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name} sliced a whole {fruit} into {total} pieces. Her {sibling1} ate {n2} more slices than her, so she ate <<n1 + n2>> slices. Her {sibling2} ate {n3} more slices than her {sibling1}, so she ate <<n1 + n2 + n3>> slices. The total number of slices they all ate is <<n1 + n2 + n3 + n1 + n2 + n3>>. The final answer is <<n1 + n2 + n3 + n1 + n2 + n3>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 56, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['alphabets', 'frac', 'n1'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 57, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. Initially, {name} writes the {alphabets} in full {n1} times, which is <<n1 * alphabets>>. Then, she writes {frac} of it once, which is <<frac * alphabets>>. After that, she re-writes everything she has already written, which is <<n1 * alphabets + frac * alphabets>>. The total number of letters written is <<n1 * alphabets + frac * alphabets>>. The final answer is <<n1 * alphabets + frac * alphabets>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 58, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['cal', 'num', 'vol'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 59, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. The total volume of {liquid} consumed is <<num * vol>> {unit}s. Since {liquid} has {cal} calories per {unit}, the total calories consumed is <<num * vol * cal>>. The final answer is <<num * vol * cal>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 60, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['b', 'd', 'h', 'r'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 61, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {name} works a {h}-hour shift each day, {d} days a week. He earns {cur}{r} per hour and gets a {cur}{b} bonus each week if the company performs well. The total hours worked in a month is <<h * d * 4>>. The total earnings from hours worked is <<h * d * 4 * 0.01 * 100>>. The total bonus is <<0.01 * 100 * 0.1 * 100>>. The total money made is <<h * d * 4 * 0.01 * 100 + 0.01 * 100 * 0.1 * 100>>. The final answer is <<h * d * 4 * 0.01 * 100 + 0.01 * 100 * 0.1 * 100>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 62, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['fake_num', 'frac', 'k', 'n'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 63, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. Initially, {name} had {n} {objects}. He dropped {frac} of them, so he lost <<n * frac>> {objects}. After dropping them, he had <<n - n * frac>> {objects}. He then picked up {k} {objects}, so he had <<n - n * frac + k>> {objects}. He inspected the {objects} further and found {fake_num} of them that weren't {objects}, but actually {fake_object}. He got rid of it, so he had <<n - n * frac + k - fake_num>> {objects}. The final answer is <<n - n * frac + k - fake_num>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 64, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['k', 'n'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 65, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. {person1} has {n} {item}s. His {relation} has {k} fewer {item}s than he has, so the relation has <<n - k>> {item}s. Together, they have <<n + (n - k)>> {item}s. The final answer is <<n + (n - k)>>.", 'iter_count': 1, 'num_backwards': 0}, {'step': 66, 'action': 'constraints_init', 'outputs': [''], 'task': 'gsm_symbolic', 'valid_vars': ['fee', 'n', 'rate'], 'backwards_limit': 20, 'max_iter': 80}, {'step': 67, 'action': 'final_output', 'outputs': [''], 'output': "Let's think step by step. If {name} does {task} herself, she'll lose <<n *